---
title: Auth - Change Password Flow (POST /auth/change-password)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client
    participant Ctrl as AuthController
    participant Guard as AuthGuard
    participant Service as AuthService
    participant AccountModel as AccountModel (TypeORM Repository)
    participant Util as Security Utils (bcrypt / crypto / jwt)
    participant DB as Database (SQL Server)

    note right of Client: POST /auth/change-password (with Bearer Token)
    Client->>Ctrl: ChangePasswordDto (oldPassword, newPassword)
    activate Ctrl
    Ctrl->>Guard: canActivate(context)
    Guard->>Util: Extract Bearer token & verify JWT
    Util-->>Guard: decodedPayload
    alt JWT is invalid / expired
        Guard-->>Client: Throw UnauthorizedException
    else JWT is valid
        Guard-->>Ctrl: Attach user to request & return true
    end
    Ctrl->>Service: changePassword(req.user.sub, dto)
    Service->>AccountModel: findOne({ accountId })
    AccountModel->>DB: SELECT * FROM Accounts WHERE AccountId = ?
    DB-->>AccountModel: row / null
    AccountModel-->>Service: Account Entity / null
    opt Account not found
        Service-->>Client: Throw BadRequestException
    end
    Service->>Util: bcrypt.compare(dto.oldPassword, account.password)
    Util-->>Service: isMatch
    opt Old password mismatch
        Service-->>Client: Throw UnauthorizedException
    end
    Service->>Util: bcrypt.hash(dto.newPassword, 10)
    Util-->>Service: newPasswordHash
    Service->>AccountModel: save(account)
    AccountModel->>DB: UPDATE Accounts SET Password = newPasswordHash WHERE AccountId = ?
    DB-->>AccountModel: ok
    Service-->>Ctrl: MessageResponseDto (message)
    deactivate Ctrl
    Ctrl-->>Client: HTTP 200 - MessageResponseDto